IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-provisions`
IMPORT `act-determinative`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory), chapter 1: Preliminary.
--
-- Part 1.1 says what this Act is part of, what it applies to, and when its provisions give way to another provision (ss 2, 2A, 4, 6).
-- Part 1.2 says what an Act, a subordinate law, a disallowable instrument, a notifiable instrument, a commencement notice,
-- a legislative instrument, a statutory instrument, an instrument, an authorised republication and a provision are (ss 7 to 16).
-- Part 1.3 adds former enactments to the meaning of "Act" (s 17).
-- Section 5 (determinative provisions) is in `act-determinative.l4`.
--
-- Where a function says "is" or "means", it answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE for every case it is given; where the text says "includes" it answers NOTHING outside the list.
-- The facts about a document that the Act does not decide (who made it, under what power) are plain inputs.

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT): chapter 1, Preliminary`

§§ `Part 1.1: General`

-- The parts of this Act that sections 2 and 2A speak of.
DECLARE `Material in this Act` IS ONE OF
    `the dictionary at the end of this Act`
    `a note included in this Act`
    `any other provision of this Act`

-- src:76 | The dictionary at the end of this Act is part of this Act.
@ref s 2 (src:76-76)
GIVEN material IS A `Material in this Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2: whether the material is part of this Act, so far as s 2 says` MEANS
    IF   material EQUALS `the dictionary at the end of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:82 | A note included in this Act is explanatory and is not part of this Act.
@ref s 2A (src:82-82)
GIVEN material IS A `Material in this Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2A: whether the material is part of this Act, so far as s 2A says` MEANS
    IF   material EQUALS `a note included in this Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- What a provision of this Act can be applied to (s 4).
DECLARE `Thing this Act might be applied to` IS ONE OF
    `an Act (including this Act)`
    `a statutory instrument`
    `something else`

-- src:98 | (1) This Act applies to all Acts (including this Act) and statutory instruments.
@ref s 4 (1) (src:98-98)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing this Act might be applied to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 (1): this Act applies to the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an Act (including this Act)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:99 | (2) In particular, Acts and statutory instruments are taken to be made on the basis that they will operate in conjunction with this Act.
@ref s 4 (2) (src:99-99)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing this Act might be applied to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 (2): the thing is taken to be made on the basis that it will operate in conjunction with this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an Act (including this Act)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

-- s 6: the facts that decide whether a provision of this Act is displaced by a provision of another Act or instrument.
-- "Contrary intention" and "manifest contrary intention" are judgments the text leaves to the reader of the two provisions; they are plain inputs.
DECLARE `Facts about a possible displacement` HAS
    `the provision of this Act is a determinative provision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other provision expressly displaces it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other provision shows a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contrary intention is manifest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the two provisions can operate concurrently` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only ground is that the two provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:119 | (1) A provision of this Act must be applied to an Act or statutory instrument, in accordance with the terms of the provision, except so far as it is displaced.
-- src:120 | (2) A determinative provision may be displaced expressly or by a manifest contrary intention.
-- src:121 | (3) A non-determinative provision may be displaced expressly or by a contrary intention.
-- src:122 | Note For the distinction between a ‘manifest contrary intention’ (see s (2)) and ‘contrary intention’ (see s (3)), see the examples in this section.
-- src:123 | (4) The declaration of a provision as ‘determinative’ indicates that it is the intention of the Legislative Assembly that, if the provision is to be displaced at all in a particular case, a more deliberate displacement is required than if the provision were a non-determinative provision.
-- src:124 | (5) This section applies despite any presumption or rule of interpretation.
-- src:125 | (6) A provision of this Act must not be taken to be displaced by a provision of an Act or statutory instrument so far as the provisions can operate concurrently.
-- src:126 | (7) In particular and without limiting subsection (6), a provision of this Act is not displaced by a provision of an Act or statutory instrument because the provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter.
@ref s 6 (1) to (3), (6), (7) (src:119-126)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts about a possible displacement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6: the provision of this Act is displaced by the other provision` MEANS
    IF   f's `the two provisions can operate concurrently`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF   f's `the only ground is that the two provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF   f's `the provision of this Act is a determinative provision`
              THEN IF   f's `the other provision expressly displaces it`
                        OR (f's `the other provision shows a contrary intention` AND f's `the contrary intention is manifest`)
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING
              ELSE IF   f's `the other provision expressly displaces it` OR f's `the other provision shows a contrary intention`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING

-- src:119 | (1) A provision of this Act must be applied to an Act or statutory instrument, in accordance with the terms of the provision, except so far as it is displaced.
@ref s 6 (1) (src:119-119)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts about a possible displacement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 (1): the provision of this Act must be applied to the Act or statutory instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 6: the provision of this Act is displaced by the other provision` f
    WHEN JUST displaced THEN JUST (NOT displaced)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 6 (4): how deliberate a displacement has to be.
DECLARE `How deliberate a displacement must be` IS ONE OF
    `a more deliberate displacement`
    `a displacement that is not more deliberate than usual`

-- src:123 | (4) The declaration of a provision as ‘determinative’ indicates that it is the intention of the Legislative Assembly that, if the provision is to be displaced at all in a particular case, a more deliberate displacement is required than if the provision were a non-determinative provision.
@ref s 6 (4) (src:123-123)
GIVEN isDeterminative IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How deliberate a displacement must be`
`s 6 (4): how deliberate a displacement of the provision must be` MEANS
    IF   isDeterminative
    THEN `a more deliberate displacement`
    ELSE `a displacement that is not more deliberate than usual`

-- src:124 | (5) This section applies despite any presumption or rule of interpretation.
@ref s 6 (5) (src:124-124)
GIVEN aPresumptionOrRuleOfInterpretationIsRelied IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6 (5): this section applies despite any presumption or rule of interpretation` MEANS TRUE

§§ `Part 1.2: Basic concepts`

-- What a provision, an enactment or an instrument is is decided from facts the Act does not itself decide: who made it and under what power.
DECLARE `Facts about an enactment or instrument` HAS
    `is a law made by the Legislative Assembly under the Self-Government Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a regulation or rule` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is any writing or other document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is made under` IS A LIST OF `Kind of Act or instrument`
    `is also made under power given otherwise by law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is declared to be a disallowable instrument by` IS A LIST OF `Kind of Act or instrument`
    `is a determination of fees or charges by a Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is declared to be a notifiable instrument by` IS A LIST OF `Kind of Act or instrument`
    `fixes or determines the commencement of` IS A LIST OF `Kind of Act or instrument`

-- Things a reference can name, for the sentences "A reference to an X includes a reference to a provision of an X".
DECLARE `Thing a reference may name` IS ONE OF
    `an Act`
    `a subordinate law`
    `a disallowable instrument`
    `a notifiable instrument`
    `a commencement notice`
    `a legislative instrument`
    `a statutory instrument`
    `an instrument`
    `an authorised republication`
    `something else`

-- src:154 | (1) An Act is an Act of the Legislative Assembly.
-- src:155 | (2) An Act of the Legislative Assembly is a law (however described or named) made by the Legislative Assembly under the Self-Government Act.
@ref s 7 (1), (2) (src:154-155)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7 (1), (2): the document is an Act` MEANS
    JUST (f's `is a law made by the Legislative Assembly under the Self-Government Act`)

-- src:161 | (1) A subordinate law is a regulation or rule (whether or not legislative in nature) made under—
-- src:162 | (a) an Act; or
-- src:163 | (b) another subordinate law; or
-- src:164 | (c) power given by an Act or subordinate law and also power given otherwise by law.
@ref s 8 (1) (src:161-164)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8 (1): the document is a subordinate law` MEANS
    JUST (f's `is a regulation or rule` AND (underAnAct OR underASubordinateLaw OR underBoth))
    WHERE
        underAnAct MEANS elem `an Act` (f's `is made under`)
        underASubordinateLaw MEANS elem `a subordinate law` (f's `is made under`)
        underBoth MEANS (underAnAct OR underASubordinateLaw) AND f's `is also made under power given otherwise by law`

-- src:168 | (1) A disallowable instrument is—
-- src:169 | (a) a statutory instrument (whether or not legislative in nature) that is declared to be a disallowable instrument by an Act, subordinate law or another disallowable instrument; or
-- src:170 | (b) a determination of fees or charges by a Minister under an Act or subordinate law.
@ref s 9 (1) (src:168-170)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9 (1): the document is a disallowable instrument` MEANS
    JUST (declared OR fees)
    WHERE
        declared MEANS
            `s 13 (1): the document is a statutory instrument` f EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND (elem `an Act` (f's `is declared to be a disallowable instrument by`)
                 OR elem `a subordinate law` (f's `is declared to be a disallowable instrument by`)
                 OR elem `a disallowable instrument` (f's `is declared to be a disallowable instrument by`))
        fees MEANS
            f's `is a determination of fees or charges by a Minister`
            AND (elem `an Act` (f's `is made under`) OR elem `a subordinate law` (f's `is made under`))

-- src:175 | (1) A notifiable instrument is a statutory instrument (whether or not legislative in nature) that is declared to be a notifiable instrument by an Act, subordinate law, disallowable instrument or another notifiable instrument.
@ref s 10 (1) (src:175-175)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10 (1): the document is a notifiable instrument` MEANS
    JUST (`s 13 (1): the document is a statutory instrument` f EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND (elem `an Act` (f's `is declared to be a notifiable instrument by`)
               OR elem `a subordinate law` (f's `is declared to be a notifiable instrument by`)
               OR elem `a disallowable instrument` (f's `is declared to be a notifiable instrument by`)
               OR elem `a notifiable instrument` (f's `is declared to be a notifiable instrument by`)))

-- src:179 | (1) A commencement notice is a statutory instrument that fixes or otherwise determines the commencement of an Act, subordinate law, disallowable instrument or notifiable instrument.
@ref s 11 (1) (src:179-179)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11 (1): the document is a commencement notice` MEANS
    JUST (`s 13 (1): the document is a statutory instrument` f EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND (elem `an Act` (f's `fixes or determines the commencement of`)
               OR elem `a subordinate law` (f's `fixes or determines the commencement of`)
               OR elem `a disallowable instrument` (f's `fixes or determines the commencement of`)
               OR elem `a notifiable instrument` (f's `fixes or determines the commencement of`)))

-- src:183 | (1) A legislative instrument is—
-- src:184 | (a) a subordinate law; or
-- src:185 | (b) a disallowable instrument; or
-- src:186 | (c) a notifiable instrument; or
-- src:187 | (d) a commencement notice.
@ref s 12 (1) (src:183-187)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12 (1): the kind of document is a legislative instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a subordinate law` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a disallowable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a commencement notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an Act` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument of another kind` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:191 | (1) A statutory instrument is an instrument (whether or not legislative in nature) made under—
-- src:192 | (a) an Act; or
-- src:193 | (b) another statutory instrument; or
-- src:194 | (c) power given by an Act or statutory instrument and also power given otherwise by law.
@ref s 13 (1) (src:191-194)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 (1): the document is a statutory instrument` MEANS
    JUST (`s 14 (1): the document is an instrument` f EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND (elem `an Act` (f's `is made under`)
               OR underAnotherStatutoryInstrument
               OR (underAnActOrStatutoryInstrument AND f's `is also made under power given otherwise by law`)))
    WHERE
        underAnotherStatutoryInstrument MEANS
            elem `a subordinate law` (f's `is made under`)
            OR elem `a disallowable instrument` (f's `is made under`)
            OR elem `a notifiable instrument` (f's `is made under`)
            OR elem `a commencement notice` (f's `is made under`)
            OR elem `a statutory instrument of another kind` (f's `is made under`)
        underAnActOrStatutoryInstrument MEANS elem `an Act` (f's `is made under`) OR underAnotherStatutoryInstrument

-- src:195 | (2) A statutory instrument includes a subordinate law, disallowable instrument, notifiable instrument and commencement notice.
@ref s 13 (2) (src:195-195)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 (2): the kind of document is included in the statutory instruments` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a subordinate law` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a disallowable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a commencement notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an Act` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a statutory instrument of another kind` THEN NOTHING

-- src:199 | (1) An instrument is any writing or other document.
@ref s 14 (1) (src:199-199)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts about an enactment or instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14 (1): the document is an instrument` MEANS
    JUST (f's `is any writing or other document`)

-- src:204 | (1) An authorised republication is a republication of a law authorised by the parliamentary counsel under this Act.
@ref s 15 (1) (src:204-204)
GIVEN isARepublicationOfALaw IS A BOOLEAN, isAuthorisedByTheParliamentaryCounselUnderThisAct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 (1): the republication is an authorised republication` MEANS
    JUST (isARepublicationOfALaw AND isAuthorisedByTheParliamentaryCounselUnderThisAct)

-- src:156 | (3) A reference to an Act includes a reference to a provision of an Act.
@ref s 7 (3) (src:156-156)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a reference may name`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7 (3): a reference to an Act includes a reference to a provision of it` MEANS
    IF   thing EQUALS `an Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:165 | (2) A reference to a subordinate law includes a reference to a provision of a subordinate law.
@ref s 8 (2) (src:165-165)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a reference may name`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8 (2): a reference to a subordinate law includes a reference to a provision of it` MEANS
    IF   thing EQUALS `a subordinate law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:172 | (2) A reference to a disallowable instrument includes a reference to a provision of a disallowable instrument.
@ref s 9 (2) (src:172-172)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a reference may name`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9 (2): a reference to a disallowable instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` MEANS
    IF   thing EQUALS `a disallowable instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:176 | (2) A reference to a notifiable instrument includes a reference to a provision of a notifiable instrument.
@ref s 10 (2) (src:176-176)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a reference may name`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10 (2): a reference to a notifiable instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` MEANS
    IF   thing EQUALS `a notifiable instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:180 | (2) A reference to a commencement notice includes a reference to a provision of a commencement notice.
@ref s 11 (2) (src:180-180)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a reference may name`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11 (2): a reference to a commencement notice includes a reference to a provision of it` MEANS
    IF   thing EQUALS `a commencement notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:188 | (2) A reference to a legislative instrument includes a reference to a provision of a legislative instrument.
@ref s 12 (2) (src:188-188)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a reference may name`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12 (2): a reference to a legislative instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` MEANS
    IF   thing EQUALS `a legislative instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:196 | (3) A reference to a statutory instrument includes a reference to a provision of a statutory instrument.
@ref s 13 (3) (src:196-196)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a reference may name`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 (3): a reference to a statutory instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` MEANS
    IF   thing EQUALS `a statutory instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:201 | (2) A reference to an instrument includes a reference to a provision of an instrument.
@ref s 14 (2) (src:201-201)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a reference may name`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14 (2): a reference to an instrument includes a reference to a provision of it` MEANS
    IF   thing EQUALS `an instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:205 | (2) A reference to an authorised republication includes a reference to a provision of an authorised republication.
@ref s 15 (2) (src:205-205)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a reference may name`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 (2): a reference to an authorised republication includes a reference to a provision of it` MEANS
    IF   thing EQUALS `an authorised republication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING


-- s 16: examples of provisions. Words, and groups of other provisions.
DECLARE `Thing in an Act or instrument` IS ONE OF
    `a section`
    `a subsection`
    `a paragraph`
    `a subparagraph`
    `a sub-subparagraph`
    `an example`
    `a chapter`
    `a part`
    `a division`
    `a subdivision`
    `a schedule`
    `something else`

DECLARE `What a provision consists of` IS ONE OF
    `a group of words`
    `a group of other provisions`

-- src:210 | A provision of an Act or instrument is any words or anything else that forms part of the Act or instrument.
@ref s 16 (src:210-210)
GIVEN formsPartOfTheActOrInstrument IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16: the words or other thing are a provision of the Act or instrument` MEANS
    JUST formsPartOfTheActOrInstrument

-- src:211 | Examples—provisions consisting of groups of words
-- src:212 | sections, subsections, paragraphs, subparagraphs, sub-subparagraphs, examples
@ref s 16, examples (provisions consisting of groups of words) (src:211-212)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing in an Act or instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE `What a provision consists of`
`s 16, examples: what the provision consists of` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `a section` THEN JUST `a group of words`
    WHEN `a subsection` THEN JUST `a group of words`
    WHEN `a paragraph` THEN JUST `a group of words`
    WHEN `a subparagraph` THEN JUST `a group of words`
    WHEN `a sub-subparagraph` THEN JUST `a group of words`
    WHEN `an example` THEN JUST `a group of words`
    WHEN `a chapter` THEN JUST `a group of other provisions`
    WHEN `a part` THEN JUST `a group of other provisions`
    WHEN `a division` THEN JUST `a group of other provisions`
    WHEN `a subdivision` THEN JUST `a group of other provisions`
    WHEN `a schedule` THEN JUST `a group of other provisions`
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Part 1.3: Sources of law in the ACT`

-- s 17: the enactments that a reference to an Act includes.
DECLARE `Kind of enactment a reference to an Act may name` IS ONE OF
    `an Act of the Legislative Assembly`
    `a former Commonwealth enactment`
    `a former NSW Act or former UK Act mentioned in schedule 1`
    `something else`

-- Schedule 1 is outside the in-scope text, so whether an Act is mentioned in it is a plain input.
DECLARE `Facts about a former enactment` HAS
    `is a Commonwealth Act or ordinance, a New South Wales Act or an Imperial Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an enactment within the meaning of the Self-Government Act because of that Act, section 34` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an enactment because of the A.C.T. Self-Government (Consequential Provisions) Act 1988 (Cwlth), section 10 (3) or section 12 (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:226 | (1) A reference to an Act includes a reference to a former Commonwealth enactment.
-- src:227 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), a reference to an Act includes a reference to a former NSW Act or former UK Act mentioned in schedule 1.
@ref s 17 (1), (2) (src:226-227)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of enactment a reference to an Act may name`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 (1), (2): a reference to an Act includes a reference to the enactment` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act of the Legislative Assembly` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a former Commonwealth enactment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a former NSW Act or former UK Act mentioned in schedule 1` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:229 | former Commonwealth enactment means a Commonwealth Act or ordinance, a New South Wales Act or Imperial Act that is—
-- src:230 | (a) an enactment within the meaning of the Self-Government Act because of that Act, section 34; or
-- src:231 | (b) an enactment because of the A.C.T. Self-Government (Consequential Provisions) Act 1988 (Cwlth), section 10 (3) or section 12 (2) or (3).
@ref s 17 (3), definition of former Commonwealth enactment (src:229-231)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts about a former enactment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 (3): the enactment is a former Commonwealth enactment` MEANS
    JUST (f's `is a Commonwealth Act or ordinance, a New South Wales Act or an Imperial Act`
          AND (f's `is an enactment within the meaning of the Self-Government Act because of that Act, section 34`
               OR f's `is an enactment because of the A.C.T. Self-Government (Consequential Provisions) Act 1988 (Cwlth), section 10 (3) or section 12 (2) or (3)`))
